body:
I think this is the closest margin-trim approximation of the quirk:
```css
body {
    margin-trin: block-start;
}
th, td {
    margin-trim: block;
}
```
This would be a superset of the current quirk in that it:
- expands the quirk to grid and flex layout<sup>[Chrome/Webkit]</sup>
- expands the quirk to horizontal BFCs
- expands the quirk to all margins, no matter the element or cascade origin

Personally not opposed to this, if it's web-compatible, which seems likely. I don't remember seeing many (any?) author-specified margins which this would get rid of when I looked at affected pages.
